cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite the arXiv version (arXiv:2109.14214), which is the
  citable form of this manuscript, and say that it has not been refereed. Cite this repository
  by URL and commit for anything that exists only here: the numerics, the figures and their
  generators, or the interactive presentation of a result.
title: >-
  Quantum simulation of conformal field theory: the revised Letter, its Supplemental
  Material, and the numerics behind every figure
abstract: >-
  A quantum algorithm for simulating the dynamics of 1+1-dimensional conformal field theory,
  including the action of local conformal transformations, built on operator-algebraic
  renormalization and the Koo-Saleur formula. Free-fermion conformal field theories of central
  charge c = 1/2 are treated in the Ramond and Neveu-Schwarz sectors, as the basis of Ising
  conformal field theories and Wess-Zumino-Witten currents. This repository holds the 2026
  revision of the manuscript, whose Supplemental Material carries a discretization error
  analysis and an explicit resource accounting: the cost is delta^{-3/2}, the product of a
  Heisenberg-limited measurement cost and a discretization cost, and the near-term figure is a
  lattice of 128 sites, that is 256 logical qubits. It also holds the version submitted in
  2022, for provenance, the scripts behind every figure, and an interactive presentation of
  the consequential results.
